Today we're releasing our newest model π0.7. It shows a similar trend that we've seen in LLMs before: we moved from fine-tuning a model to just prompting it, bringing us one step closer to a model that can control any robot to do any task.

@physical_int: "Our newest model, π0.7, has some interesting emergent capabilities: it can control a new robot to fold shirts for which we had no shirt folding data, figure out how to use an appliance with language-based coaching, and perform a wide range of dexterous tasks all in one model!"

Physical Intelligence is working on bringing general-purpose AI into the physical world.

LLM post-training used to mean fine-tuning to a downstream task, and robotics has been stuck in this setting, needing task-specific fine-tuning for best performance. π07 changes this by working out of the box and outperforming fine-tuned specialists.

